 "displayField": "MED2014_V1_00_NAME",
 "description": "<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>MED</span><SPAN>2014_V1_00 is </span><SPAN>the definitive set of M</span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN>ori electoral district boundaries as defined by the Electoral Commission</span><SPAN> </span><SPAN>as at </span><SPAN STYLE=\"font-weight:bold;\">17 April 2014</span><SPAN>.</span><SPAN> </span><SPAN>Land Information New Zealand (LINZ) and Statistics New Zealand are the custodians. </span></p><P><SPAN /><SPAN /></p><P><SPAN><SPAN>These districts comprise the M</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori electoral districts as constituted under the Electoral Act 1993.</span></span></p><P><P><SPAN><SPAN>M</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori electorate boundaries are defined at meshblock level. The number of M</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori electoral districts, and electoral populations for each electorate</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>,</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>is controlled by criteria in the Electoral Act. Within these criteria, when setting the boundaries, the Representation Commission also consider the existing boundaries of the M</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori electoral districts, community of interest among the M</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori people generally and members of iwi, facilities of communications, topographical features, and any projected variation in the M</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori electoral population of those districts during their existence</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>.</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>The Representation Commission is convened by the Surveyor-General every five years, followin</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>g a population census and Mā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori Electoral Option. Its role is to re-draw electoral boundaries to follow prescribed population quotas.</span></span></p><P><SPAN>M</span><SPAN>ā</span><SPAN>ori </span><SPAN>electoral districts </span><SPAN /><SPAN>are reviewed and redrawn after </span><SPAN>the </span><SPAN>Census of Population and </span><SPAN>Dwellings is undertaken</span><SPAN>. These boundaries are then used for the next two general elections</span></p><P><SPAN><SPAN>M</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN>ori electoral district is a flat classification </span><SPAN>and </span><SPAN>contains </span><SPAN STYLE=\"font-weight:bold;\">7 </span><SPAN>Māori electoral districts</span><SPAN>, there are 8 Māori electoral districts including 1 Māori electoral district classified as \"Area Outside Māori Electoral District'.</span></p><P><SPAN><SPAN>The following table lists the 2014 Mā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori </span></span><SPAN>electoral districts:</span></p><TABLE><TBODY><TR><TD><P><SPAN>Māori </span><SPAN>electoral district code</span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Mā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori </span></span><SPAN><SPAN>electoral district label</span></span></p></td></tr><TR><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>1</span></span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Hauraki-Waikato</span></span></p></td></tr><TR><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>2</span></span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Ikaroa-Rā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>whiti</span></span></p></td></tr><TR><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>3</span></span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Tā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>maki Makaurau</span></span></p></td></tr><TR><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>4</span></span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Te Tai Hauā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>uru</span></span></p></td></tr><TR><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>5</span></span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Te Tai Tokerau</span></span></p></td></tr><TR><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>6</span></span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Te Tai Tonga</span></span></p></td></tr><TR><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>7</span></span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Waiariki</span></span></p></td></tr><TR><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>9</span></span></p></td><TD><P><SPAN><SPAN>Area Outside Mā</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ori </span></span><SPAN><SPAN>Electoral District</span></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><P><P><SPAN><SPAN>M</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>ā</span></span><SPAN>ori electoral district boundaries are defined at meshblock level. </span></p><P><SPAN><SPAN>Digital boundary data became freely available on 1 July 2007</span></span><SPAN><SPAN>.</span></span></p><P><SPAN /></p><P><SPAN>ArcGIS and MapInfo formats do not support the use of macrons. Macrons have applied to the following Maori electorate names:</span></p><UL><LI><P><SPAN>Ikaroa-Râwhiti</span></p></li><LI><P><SPAN>Tâmaki Makaurau</span></p></li><LI><P><SPAN>Te Tai Hauâuru</span></p></li></ul><P><SPAN /></p><P><SPAN /></p></div></div></div></p></p>",
